{"requirements":[{"id":"source_of_truth_and_final_sync","requirement":"Use node1 `/etc/inventory/app.conf` as the authoritative source and maintain a matching copy on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node2 synchronization script fetches only node1's file through a source-IP-bound, forced read-only SSH command. Final source and target SHA-256 values match, including after both node restarts, and node2 has appropriate root ownership and mode 0644.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dcb99d55861948db","cmd-92af6715fad24438","cmd-d35914b734e14bf0","cmd-500725f698704245","cmd-513a5b0e89104f54"]},{"id":"automatic_sync_within_15_minutes","requirement":"Automatically pick up changes from node1 on node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"An enabled persistent timer is configured for approximately five-minute intervals and ran autonomously after node2 restarted. A real source change reached node2 in six seconds with identical content, but that propagation was initiated by explicitly starting the service rather than waiting for the timer. Thus synchronization works and the schedule supports the deadline, but automatic propagation of changed content within the bound was not directly demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af031202202543c1","cmd-ece5a9b3219c4a6a","cmd-c8c629ce04e146a7","cmd-3640309e58b44f93","cmd-500725f698704245"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the initially absent source file, restricted SSH credentials, synchronization script, and systemd units directly supported the task; the probe change was bounded evidence and was fully removed; manual service starts collected bounded verification; and both reboot actions were required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The final snapshots show no failed services, no new listening ports, healthy package state, and only expected reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d51812e898914fc7","cmd-9c2ab216da22451d","cmd-dcb99d55861948db","cmd-92af6715fad24438","cmd-ece5a9b3219c4a6a","cmd-f6d7995b2faf4620","cmd-c2a2b382a7714655","cmd-98721b197b624489","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The source-authoritative synchronization implementation is functional, persistent, and recovered cleanly through sequential restarts. The only material evidence gap is that the changed-content test used a manual service start; the timer itself ran automatically after reboot, but no captured test showed it autonomously detecting a new change within 15 minutes. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on both nodes, with pre-restart health, acknowledgements, changed boot identities, and recovered system, service, data, and synchronization state.","limitations":["Automatic changed-content propagation was not observed end-to-end through a scheduled timer firing; its 15-minute bound is supported by timer configuration and separate autonomous post-reboot execution rather than one direct transition.","Lifecycle snapshots cover general system health but do not inventory the task-specific files or systemd definitions; their final state is established by executor command evidence.","The initial source file was absent, so the executor created minimal baseline content; no authored baseline specified what its initial application content should contain."]}
